/T (mBERT achieves 75.13% accuracy and 0.7476 macro F1 on Croatian hate speech, substantially higher than the English results. This is largely explained by the task difference: Croatian is a binary classification \(acceptable vs unacceptable\), while English is a three-class problem with an ambiguous middle class. The character n-gram TF-IDF baseline is stronger on Croatian \(0.7592 F1\) than word-level baselines on English, confirming the suitability of character-level features for morphologically rich languages.)
/E (mBERT achieves 75.13% accuracy and 0.7476 macro F1 on Croatian hate speech, substantially higher than the English results. This is largely explained by the task difference: Croatian is a binary classification \(acceptable vs unacceptable\), while English is a three-class problem with an ambiguous middle class. The character n-gram TF-IDF baseline is stronger on Croatian \(0.7592 F1\) than word-level baselines on English, confirming the suitability of character-level features for morphologically rich languages.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
