290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 43 0 R
/T (All three bonus objectives were also achieved: three models were compared, the multilingual experiment extended the work to Croatian, and a soft-voting ensemble was implemented as the advanced technique. The ensemble achieved the best performance overall \(70.11% accuracy, 0.6911 macro F1\), confirming that combining complementary models reduces individual errors. The central finding is that the offensive class represents a persistent and fundamental challenge that cannot be fully resolved by model scale alone. Domain-specific pretraining and class-aware training strategies both help, but the semantic overlap between classes remains the primary bottleneck. Future work should focus on richer supervision signals and larger domain-specific models.)
/E (All three bonus objectives were also achieved: three models were compared, the multilingual experiment extended the work to Croatian, and a soft-voting ensemble was implemented as the advanced technique. The ensemble achieved the best performance overall \(70.11% accuracy, 0.6911 macro F1\), confirming that combining complementary models reduces individual errors. The central finding is that the offensive class represents a persistent and fundamental challenge that cannot be fully resolved by model scale alone. Domain-specific pretraining and class-aware training strategies both help, but the semantic overlap between classes remains the primary bottleneck. Future work should focus on richer supervision signals and larger domain-specific models.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 43 0 R
/T (This project successfully implemented the complete fine-tuning pipeline for pretrained transformer models on a multiclass hate speech detection task. All assignment requirements were met: transformer theory was presented, a public dataset was selected and described, preprocessing was justified, three transformer models were fine-tuned with documented hyperparameters, results were evaluated using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score, confusion matrices and learning curves were visualized, and a comparison with a classical baseline was provided.)
/E (This project successfully implemented the complete fine-tuning pipeline for pretrained transformer models on a multiclass hate speech detection task. All assignment requirements were met: transformer theory was presented, a public dataset was selected and described, preprocessing was justified, three transformer models were fine-tuned with documented hyperparameters, results were evaluated using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score, confusion matrices and learning curves were visualized, and a comparison with a classical baseline was provided.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
