600 0 obj
<<
/Title (Fine-tuning is the process of continuing the training of a pretrained transformer on a task-specific labeled dataset. The model adapts its internal representations to the target classification objective while retaining its linguistic prior. This allows strong performance even on relatively small datasets, and is the central methodology demonstrated in this project.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 544 0 R
>>
endobj
601 0 obj
<<
/Title (HateXplain is a publicly available dataset for hate speech analysis hosted on Hugging Face \(Hate-speech-CNERG/hatexplain\). It contains 19,229 social media posts from Gab and Twitter, each annotated by three human annotators with one of three labels: hateful \(0\), normal \(1\), or offensive \(2\). The final label is determined by majority vote. The dataset provides official train/validation/test splits. The class distribution in the training set is: normal \(40.64%\), hateful \(30.87%\), and offensive \(28.50%\). This moderate imbalance was handled through class-weighted loss functions in transformer experiments and class-weighted Logistic Regression in the baseline. Text lengths range from 2 to 165 words \(median: 21 words\), guiding the choice of max_length=128 tokens.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 546 0 R
>>
endobj
602 0 obj
<<
