609 0 obj
<<
/Title (mBERT achieves 75.13% accuracy and 0.7476 macro F1 on Croatian hate speech, substantially higher than the English results. This is largely explained by the task difference: Croatian is a binary classification \(acceptable vs unacceptable\), while English is a three-class problem with an ambiguous middle class. The character n-gram TF-IDF baseline is stronger on Croatian \(0.7592 F1\) than word-level baselines on English, confirming the suitability of character-level features for morphologically rich languages.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 550 0 R
/Prev 608 0 R
>>
endobj
