/Title (Transformer models are encoder architectures based on the self-attention mechanism, which allows each word to be represented in the context of all other words in the input sequence. This contextual representation is far richer than traditional bag-of-words or TF-IDF approaches, which treat words independently. Models such as BERT, RoBERTa, and DistilBERT are first pretrained on massive unlabeled text corpora to acquire broad linguistic knowledge.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 599 0 R
>>
